      "properties": { "Node name for S&R": "CLIPTextEncode" },
      "widgets_values": ["Vintage woodcut illustration of a Florida Manatee Zone warning sign mounted on two weathered wooden pilings rising from calm water. The sign is white with an orange border. Text reads 'MANATEE ZONE' small at top, 'SLOW SPEED' large in the middle, 'MINIMUM WAKE' below it in bold block letters. A bold plain red circle -- no slash, no line through it, just a clean circle outline -- sits prominently on the sign face. Pilings are weathered, barnacled, slightly crooked. Water laps gently at the base. Mangroves suggested in the far background. Rendered in loose woodcut style, confident ink lines, hand-drawn feel, slightly worn. Four colors only -- cream background, dark navy illustration, orange on the sign border, red circle on the sign face only. Flat color, no gradients, no airbrush, no photoreal shading, screen-print-ready linework. Below the illustration: 'ADMIRALS COVE -- JUPITER, FL' in small condensed serif. No frame, no border around the whole graphic. Feels like an illustration from a 1970s Florida boating safety manual. Print-ready for back of a cream Comfort Colors heavyweight tee."]
